          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "row",
          "valign": "center",
          "items": [
            {
              "type": "stack",
              "flex": 9,
              "items": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "html": "<h2>Artificial Intelligence Face Attribute Tool</h2><div>This application allows the user to specify different regions to focus on, as well as including an AI model that can be used to determine the attributes automatically with a positive detection threshold.</div><ul class=\"tags\"><li>Machine learning</li><li>Computer vision</li></ul>"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "stack",
              "flex": 11,
              "items": [
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "src": "assets/maya-scripts/04.png",
                  "width": 1005,
                  "ratio": 0.5683,
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "gallery",
                  "items": [
                    {
                      "type": "image",
                      "src": "assets/maya-scripts/03.png",
                      "width": 821,
                      "ratio": 0.415,
                      "caption": null
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "row",
          "valign": "center",
          "items": [
            {
              "type": "stack",
              "flex": 3,
              "items": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "html": "<h2>OpenGL Particle Physics Simulation</h2><div>Physically based movement and collisions. These objects and particles move with forces acting upon them such as wind force, gravity, mass, wind resistance, friction, and elasticity.</div><ul class=\"tags\"><li>OpenGL</li></ul>"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "stack",
              "flex": 2,
              "items": [
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "src": "assets/maya-scripts/06.gif",
                  "width": 600,
                  "ratio": 1,
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "gallery",
                  "items": [
                    {
                      "type": "image",
                      "src": "assets/maya-scripts/05.gif",
                      "width": 600,
                      "ratio": 1,
                      "caption": null
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "row",
          "valign": "center",
          "items": [
            {
              "type": "stack",
              "flex": 3,
              "items": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "html": "<h2>Maya Python Planet Generation Tool</h2><div>This script was made to generate planets using height maps. The script can take a height map, wrap it to an object, and then map the hue values from the height map to a given vertex. Add some water and you got a planet!</div><div><a href=\"https://github.com/AlecCromer/MayaScripts/blob/master/height_map_to_geometry.py\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">The full code can be found here on GitHub</a></div><ul class=\"tags\"><li>Maya</li><li>Python</li></ul>"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "stack",
              "flex": 2,
              "items": [
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "src": "assets/maya-scripts/07.gif",
                  "width": 540,
                  "ratio": 1,
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "gallery",
                  "items": [
                    {
                      "type": "image",
                      "src": "assets/maya-scripts/08.png",
                      "width": 1081,
                      "ratio": 1,
                      "caption": null
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "row",
          "valign": "center",
          "items": [
            {
              "type": "stack",
              "flex": 9,
              "items": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "html": "<h2>Voronoi Normal Map Generator / Viewer</h2><div>A tool that generates normal maps from Voronoi cell patterns, with a viewer to preview how the map shades a surface under moving light.</div><ul class=\"tags\"><li>Normal maps</li><li>Procedural textures</li></ul>"
